      "writtenOn": "2020-04-01T23:49:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The states are externally defined by the PD spec, not just an internal implementation detail, that\u0027s one of the things I like about TCPMv2, so we are checking we have implemented the spec correctly, which seems like a good thing to me.\n\nIf you really don\u0027t want the direct connection, then how about a mapping from internal state to external PD spec state to decouple them? Then do something like:\nTEST_ASSERT(pd_spec_state(PORT0) \u003d\u003d PD_SPEC_ATTACH_WAIT_SNK)\n\nI feel like not having any access to the state makes it more inconvenient and error prone to write tests, which will lead to fewer tests.",
